\p In¦221835 the month¦221835 of¦221835 Kislev¦221837 during the twentieth¦221840 year¦221839 \add of the reign of King Artahshashta (Artaxerxes) over the Persian Empire\add*, I¦221841 was¦221842 in¦221835 the capital city of¦221839 Shushan¦221843 \add !(Susa¦221843)\add*.
\v 2 Hanani¦221847, one¦221848 of¦221849 my¦221849 brothers¦221849, came¦221846 \add ≈with some other\add* men¦221851 from¦221852 Yehudah¦221852, and¦221853 I¦221853 asked¦221853 them¦221853 about the¦221856 Jews¦221856 who'd escaped¦221857 \add ≈and managed to avoid being exiled\add*, and about Yerushalem¦221866,
\v 3 and¦221868 he told¦221868 me¦221869, “The ones left¦221870 behind in¦221878 the provinces¦221878 and who¦221870 \add ≈avoided\add* the¦221876 captivity¦221876, are¦221879 in \add ≈a bad way and feeling depressed\add*. The¦221882 wall¦221882 around Yerushalem¦221883 was¦221884 torn¦221884 down¦221884, and¦221885 its¦221885 gates¦221885 were¦221886 burnt¦221886.”
\p
\v 4 When¦221889 I heard¦221890 \add ≈all that\add*, I sat¦221896 down¦221896 and I \add ≈was¦221889 upset for days¦221899\add*. I fasted¦221901 and cried¦221897 and prayed¦221902 to¦221903 the god¦221904 of¦221903 the heavens¦221905,
\v 5 and¦221907 I said¦221907, “Oh¦221909 Yahweh¦221909, God¦221910 of¦221910 the¦221911 heavens¦221911, the great¦221913 and¦221914 awesome¦221914 God, who¦221915 keeps¦221915 \add &his¦221916\add* agreement¦221916 and¦221917 \add ≈is determinedly loyal¦221917\add* to¦221918 those¦221918 who¦221918 love¦221918 him¦221918 and¦221919 \add ≈obey his instructions¦221920\add*:
\v 6 Please¦221923 listen¦221930 \add ≈carefully\add* to¦221931 your¦221934 servant's¦221934 prayer¦221933 that¦221935 I'm \add ≈presenting to¦221938 you\add* today, day¦221939 and¦221941 night¦221941, on¦221942 account of your¦221946 servants¦221946 the¦221950 \add ≈Israelis\add*. \add ≈On¦221942 behalf of all Israelis¦221945\add*, I'm confessing¦221947 that¦221954 we've¦221955 sinned¦221955 against you—\add ≈both my generation and previous generations\add*.
\v 7 We've acted¦221964 extremely corruptly¦221964—\add ≈disobeying\add* you by not¦221966 \add ≈obeying your\add* commands¦221971, statutes¦221974, and¦221975 judgements¦221977 that¦221978 you¦221979 \add ≈instructed¦221979 through\add* your servant¦221983 Mosheh¦221982.
\v 8 Please¦221987 remember¦221985 \add ≈that¦221991 you¦221992 told¦221992\add* your¦221996 servant¦221996 Mosheh¦221995 \add ≈that if we act¦221999 unfaithfully¦221999, you yourself would¦222001 scatter¦222001 us\add* among¦222003 the¦221990 nations¦222003,\x + \xo 1:8: \xt Lev 26:33.\x*
\v 9 \add ≈but¦222005 if we'd return¦222005 to¦222006 you and¦222007 obey your instructions¦222008, then¦222005 even if¦222011 we had¦222025 been¦222013 banished¦222014 to the¦222015 ends¦222015 of¦222015 the¦222016 earth, you'd gather¦222018 us back up and¦222019 bring¦222019 us back to¦222021 the¦222023 place¦222023 where¦222024 you've established your name¦222029 and reputation¦222029\add*.\x + \xo 1:9: \xt Deu 30:1-5.\x*
\p
\v 10 “\add ≈We're your\add* servants¦222033 and¦222032 your people¦222034 that you¦222036 \add ≈rescued from slavery\add* with¦222037 your¦222037 \add ≈incredible¦222038 power¦222037\add*.
\v 11 Oh, my¦222043 master¦222043, please¦222045 \add ≈listen¦222048 carefully\add* to¦222049 your¦222052 servant's¦222052 prayer, and¦222053 to¦222053 the prayer¦222055 of¦222055 your¦222056 \add other\add* servants¦222056 who delight¦222057 to¦222058 \add ≈honour\add* your name¦222061. Please¦222042 cause your¦222046 servant to succeed¦222062 today, and¦222067 give¦222067 \add ≈me favour in¦222069 the king's¦222075 eyes\add*.”
\p Now as for me, I¦222072 was¦222073 the¦222055 king's cupbearer.
\c 2
