\p
\v 1 All¦225149 the¦225151 people¦225151 gathered¦225148 \add ≈together in¦225158 the¦225159 plaza near\add* the¦225161 Water¦225161 Gate¦225159 and¦225162 \add ≈asked¦225162\add* Ezra¦225163 the¦225164 scribe¦225164 to¦225165 bring¦225165 the¦225168 scroll¦225168 with \add ≈Yahweh's¦225174 instructions¦225173 to Yisrael¦225177 given through\add* Mosheh¦225170 \add !(Moses¦225170)\add*.
\v 2 \add ≈So¦225179 it was the beginning of October when\add* Ezra¦225180 the¦225181 priest¦225181 brought¦225179 the¦225184 \add ≈scroll\add* to¦225185 the gathering¦225186 of men¦225187 and¦225188 women¦225190 and¦225191 everyone¦225195 who¦225192 wanted to understand¦225192 it,
\v 3 and¦225199 he¦225199 \add ≈read it¦225199 aloud in the plaza near\add* the Water¦225209 Gate¦225207—reading from¦225210 dawn until¦225213 the¦225215 middle¦225215 of¦225215 the¦225216 day¦225216 in front¦225202 of those¦225220 men¦225218 and¦225219 women¦225219 and \add ≈interested people¦225224, who¦225220 all¦225222 listened intently\add*.
\p
\v 4 Ezra¦225231 the¦225232 scribe¦225232 stood on¦225233 a raised wooden¦225237 platform¦225235 that¦225238 they had¦225239 made¦225239 \add ≈especially for this purpose\add*. Standing¦225241 on his right¦225251 were¦225252 Mattitiah¦225243, Shema¦225244, Anayah¦225245, Uriyah¦225246, Hilkiyah¦225247, and Ma'aseyah, and on his left¦225252 stood Pedayah¦225253, Misha'el¦225254, Malkiyah¦225255, Hashum¦225256, Hashbaddanah¦225257, Zekaryah¦225258, and Meshullam¦225259.
\p
\v 5 \add ≈Up¦225277 on¦225277 the platform¦225277,\add* Ezra¦225263 opened¦225262 the¦225264 \add ≈scroll¦225264 in front\add* of¦225265 all the people, and¦225276 \add ≈as¦225276 he¦225276 did so\add*, all¦225278 the people stood¦225277 up¦225277.
\v 6 Ezra¦225283 blessed¦225282 the great¦225288 God Yahweh and¦225289 the¦225292 people¦225292 \add ≈raised¦225296 their arms and responded¦225289\add*, “May it¦225282 be so.” Then¦225282 they¦225298 knelt down¦225299 and bowed¦225298 to Yahweh \add ≈with¦225296 their¦225297 faces¦225301\add* to the ground¦225302.
\p
\v 7 Then¦225304 Yeshua¦225304, Bani¦225305, Shereveyah¦225306, Yamin¦225310, Akkub¦225311, Shabtai¦225312, Hodiyyah¦225314, Ma'aseyah, Kelita¦225316, Azaryah¦225317, Yozavad¦225318, Hanan¦225319, Pelayah¦225320, who were¦225322 all Levites¦225321, \add ≈explained what had been read\add* to¦225322 the¦225325 people¦225325 standing there.
\v 8 They¦225332 read¦225332 the scroll¦225333 containing God's¦225335 instructions¦225334, \add ≈explaining how it applied so\add* the people could understand¦225339 \add *it\add*.
\p
\v 9 Then Nehemyah¦225344 the¦225346 governor¦225346 and¦225347 Ezra¦225347 the¦225348 priest¦225348 & scribe¦225350, and¦225351 the¦225351 Levites¦225351 who¦225352 were \add ≈explaining it\add*, said¦225343 to all¦225356 the¦225358 people¦225358, “Today is¦225360 a sacred¦225360 day¦225359—it¦225362 belongs to¦225363 your god¦225364 Yahweh¦225363. Don't¦225365 mourn¦225367 or weep¦225370.” \add That was\add* because¦225371 all¦225373 the people were¦225372 weeping¦225372 after they¦225376 heard¦225376 \add ≈Yahweh's¦225363 instructions¦225380 to them\add*.
\v 10 Then¦225382 \add @Nehemyah¦225405\add* told¦225382 them¦225383, “Go¦225384 \add home and\add* eat¦225385 \add ≈some special food¦225386 with sweet¦225388 drink¦225387\add*, and¦225389 \add ≈share some with\add* those \add ≈who can't¦225399 afford such things¦225388\add* because¦225394 today is¦225396 \add ≈a¦225392 sacred¦225396 day¦225397 that\add* belongs to¦225398 our¦225398 master¦225398. And¦225399 don't¦225399 grieve¦225401, because¦225402 \add ≈the¦225404 happiness from Yahweh¦225398 will make you all strong\add*.”
\p
