\rem /s1 The People Confess Their Sins; National Confession; The Israelites Confess Their Sins
\p
\v 1 On¦225590 the 24th of¦225596 that¦225594 month¦225593, the \add ≈Israelis¦225598 dressed in¦225590 sackcloth¦225600, put dust on¦225590 their heads, fasted¦225599, and¦225600 gathered¦225595 together\add*.
\v 2 Those of \add ≈Jewish descent stood¦225610 separately¦225604\add* from¦225607 the¦225605 descendants¦225605 of foreigners¦225609, and¦225604 they¦225604 confessed¦225611 their \add own\add* sins¦225614, as well as those of their ancestors¦225616.
\v 3 They¦225618 stood¦225618 and¦225622 \add ≈listened to the¦225623 scroll¦225623 with¦225623 Yahweh's¦225625 instructions¦225624 being read¦225622 for three hours\add*, then¦225618 for \add ≈another three hours\add* they¦225630 confessed¦225630 and¦225631 bowed¦225631 down¦225631 to¦225632 Yahweh¦225632 their¦225633 god¦225626.
\v 4 Then Yeshua¦225641 went up¦225636 the¦225639 Levites¦225640' stairs with¦225650 Bani, Kadmi'el, Shevanyah¦225644, Bunni¦225645, Shereveyah¦225646, \add another\add* Bani¦225647, \add and\add* Kenani¦225648, and¦225649 they¦225649 called¦225649 out¦225649 loudly to¦225652 their¦225655 god¦225655 Yahweh¦225654.
\p
\v 5 Then¦225657 \add ≈some\add* Levites¦225658 (Yeshua¦225659, Kadmi'el, Bani¦225661, Hashavneyah¦225662, Shereveyah¦225663, Hodiyyah¦225664, Shevanyah¦225665, and Petahyah¦225666) said¦225657, “\add ≈Stand\add* up \add and\add* bless¦225668 your eternal¦225678 God¦225672 Yahweh¦225671: May¦225679 \add @the¦225680 peoples¦225679\add* bless your \add ≈wonderful reputation¦225680\add* which is¦225682 \add ≈greater than anything else that we bless¦225687 or praise¦225688\add*.
\rem /s1 The Prayer of Confession
\v 6 Yahweh¦225693, you alone¦225694 are¦225693 \add @God¦225692\add*. You yourself¦225694 made¦225697 the¦225700 heavens¦225700, the¦225701 \add ≈galaxies in\add* the¦225702 heavens¦225702 and¦225703 all¦225703 their¦225705 \add ≈stars\add*, the¦225706 earth¦225706 and¦225707 all¦225707 that¦225709 is on¦225710 it, the¦225711 seas¦225711 and¦225712 all¦225712 that¦225714 is¦225715 in¦225715 them¦225715. You \add ≈give life¦225717 to everything\add*, and \add ≈all the stars bow¦225724 down¦225724\add* to you.
\p
\v 7 “You¦225732 are¦225729 Yahweh¦225729, the¦225730 god who¦225731 chose¦225732 Abram¦225733. Then you¦225734 brought¦225734 him¦225734 out¦225734 from¦225735 Ur¦225735 in¦225733 the¦225736 \add ≈Chaldean region\add*, then you¦225737 \add ≈renamed him to\add* Abraham¦225739 \add (meaning ‘father of many’)\add*.
\v 8 You¦225741 \add ≈discovered¦225741 that he was sincere and faithful¦225745 to¦225746 you, and made¦225747 an agreement¦225749 with¦225748 him¦225748\add*—to¦225750 give¦225750 the Canaanite¦225754, Hittite¦225755, Amorite¦225756, Perizzite¦225757, Yebusite¦225758, and¦225759 the¦225759 Girgashite¦225759 \add ≈regions¦225753\add* to his¦225761 descendants¦225761, and you have \add ≈ensured that it's¦225748 all come to be\add* because¦225766 you're righteous¦225767.\x + \xo 9:8: \xt Gen 15:18-21.\x*
\v 9 You¦225779 \add ≈noticed¦225770 the¦225773 suffering¦225773\add* of our¦225774 ancestors¦225774 \add enslaved\add* in¦225775 Egypt¦225775, and¦225776 then¦225770 you¦225779 heard¦225779 their¦225778 cry¦225778 \add for help\add* \add ≈at¦225775 the edge of¦225778\add* the¦225782 Red Sea¦225782.
\p
\v 10 “You¦225798 \add ≈displayed miracles¦225787\add* to Far-oh¦225789 \add !(Pharaoh¦225789)\add*, and¦225790 to all¦225790 his¦225792 servants¦225792 and¦225793 to all¦225793 the¦225795 \add ≈Egyptian\add* people¦225795, because¦225797 you knew¦225798 that¦225807 they¦225800 were acting¦225800 \add ≈as¦225806 if¦225799 you weren't real\add*, \add ≈so you got yourself¦225804 a reputation¦225805 which¦225799 you still have¦225800 to¦225804\add* this¦225807 day¦225806.\x + \xo 9:10: \xt Exo 7:8–12:32.\x*
\v 11 Then¦225809 you¦225810 split¦225810 the sea open¦225810 the sea \add ≈right in front¦225811 of their eyes\add*, and¦225809 they¦225812 \add ≈walked¦225812\add* through the¦225813 middle¦225813 of \add *it\add* on¦225813 dry land¦225816. \add ≈After that,\add* you \add ≈drowned\add* their pursuers¦225819 into¦225821 the¦225821 \add ≈deep sea\add* like¦225822 a stone¦225824 in \add ≈a huge lake¦225809\add*.\x + \xo 9:11: a \xt Exo 14:21-29; \xo b \xt Exo 15:4-5.\x*
\v 12 You¦225830 led¦225830 them¦225830 \add ≈during the\add* day¦225831 with a pillar of cloud¦225829, and¦225832 \add ≈during¦225832 the\add* night¦225834 with a pillar of fire¦225833 to¦225835 illuminate¦225835 the¦225839 way¦225839 that¦225840 they¦225841 should go.\x + \xo 9:12: \xt Exo 13:21-22.\x*
\p
\v 13 “Then¦225845 you¦225849 came¦225849 down¦225849 to Mt¦225846. Sinai¦225848 and¦225850 spoke¦225850 with¦225851 them¦225851 from¦225852 the¦225846 sky¦225852, and¦225853 you gave¦225853 to¦225854 them¦225854 \add ≈principles of justice¦225855\add* and¦225857 laws¦225857 of¦225857 truth¦225858—good¦225861 statutes¦225859 and instructions¦225859.\x + \xo 9:13-14: \xt Exo 19:18–23:33.\x*
\v 14 You¦225867 \add ≈revealed the¦225865 concept of¦225865 a rest day\add* to¦225869 them¦225869, and you¦225873 \add ≈gave\add* them rules¦225871 and¦225872 instructions¦225873 and laws¦225872 via your¦225866 servant¦225877 Mosheh¦225876 \add !(Moses¦225876)\add*.
\p
\v 15 “You¦225881 gave¦225881 them bread¦225879 from¦225885 the sky¦225880 \add ≈when they were hungry¦225883\add*, and¦225879 you \add ≈made\add* water¦225884 \add ≈come¦225891 out of¦225888 a rock¦225885 when they were thirsty¦225888\add*, then¦225879 \add eventually\add* you¦225886 told¦225889 them¦225890 to¦225891 go¦225891 \add ≈ahead\add* to¦225892 possess¦225892 the¦225895 land¦225895 that you¦225898 had¦225898 \add ≈said¦225889 that you'd\add* give¦225902 to¦225903 them¦225903.\x + \xo 9:15: a \xt Exo 16:4-15; \xo b \xt Exo 17:1-7; \xo c \xt Deu 1:21.\x*
\p
\v 16 “\add ≈But¦225905\add* our¦225906 ancestors¦225906 \add ≈were proud and¦225908 stubborn\add* and¦225912 they¦225913 \add ≈refused to¦225914 obey your¦225916 instructions¦225916\add*.\x + \xo 9:16-17: \xt Num 14:1-4; Deu 1:26-33.\x*
\v 17 \add ≈Not¦225920 only did¦225925 they refuse¦225918 to¦225919 listen¦225919\add*, they¦225922 \add ≈forgot about¦225923 all the miracles¦225923 that¦225924 you'd done¦225925 for\add* them¦225926 and¦225927 they¦225927 \add ≈became stubborn\add* and¦225931 appointed¦225931 a leader¦225933 to¦225934 take them back to¦225935 their¦225935 slavery¦225935. \add ≈But¦225918\add* you¦225925 are¦225938 a god¦225938 of¦225936 forgiveness¦225939—gracious¦225940 and¦225941 compassionate¦225941, \add ≈slow to get angry¦225944\add* and \add ≈generously showing loyal affection\add*, and you didn't¦225920 abandon¦225951 them¦225951.\x + \xo 9:17: \xt Exo 34:6; Num 14:18.\x*
\v 18 Even¦225953 when they¦225956 \add ≈molded a metal¦225959\add* calf¦225958 for¦225957 themselves and¦225960 said¦225960, ‘This¦225961 is¦225962 your¦225962 god¦225962 who¦225963 brought¦225964 you \add ≈out of¦225958\add* Egypt¦225965’, and¦225966 they¦225966 \add ≈badly insulted you\add*,\x + \xo 9:18: \xt Exo 32:1-4.\x*
\v 19 you¦225974 didn't abandon¦225974 them in¦225971 the wilderness¦225975 \add ≈because you're so merciful\add*. \add ≈You¦225974 didn't remove\add* the¦225978 pillar¦225978 of¦225978 cloud¦225979 that led¦225985 them on¦225971 the way \add ≈during¦225975 the¦225979\add* day¦225984, or \add ≡remove\add* the pillar¦225989 of¦225989 fire¦225990 that shone at¦225971 night¦225991 for¦225993 them \add ≈to¦225985 show them\add* which¦225997 way they¦225998 should go.\x + \xo 9:19-21: \xt Deu 8:2-4.\x*
\v 20 You gave them your¦226002 good¦226003 spirit¦226002 to¦226005 give them¦226005 insight. You didn't¦226007 withhold¦226009 your manna¦226006 \add ≈for¦226013 them to eat\add*, and¦226002 you¦226009 \add still\add* gave them water¦226011 \add ≈to drink\add*,
\v 21 \add yes,\add* you¦226018 sustained¦226018 them¦226018 in¦226019 the wilderness¦226019 for forty¦226016 years¦226017—they \add ≈had everything they needed\add*—their clothes¦226022 didn't wear¦226024 out¦226024, and¦226016 their¦226022 feet¦226025 didn't swell¦226027.
\p
\v 22 “Then¦226029 you \add ≈handed¦226029 kingdoms¦226031 and¦226032 people¦226032 groups over to¦226030\add* them¦226030, and¦226033 you¦226033 \add ≈let them¦226033 settle in even the far corners¦226034 of the regions¦226038\add*. They¦226035 took¦226035 possession¦226035 of the King Sihon's¦226039 Heshbon¦226044 \add ≈region\add*, and¦226045 King Og's¦226048 Bashan¦226051 \add ≈region\add*.\x + \xo 9:22: \xt Num 21:21-35.\x*
\v 23 You¦226054 \add ≈gave our ancestors lots of children¦226053 so\add* they were like¦226055 the¦226055 \add many\add* stars¦226055 in the¦226056 sky¦226056, then¦226053 you¦226057 brought¦226057 them¦226057 into¦226058 this land¦226060 which¦226061 you'd told¦226063 their¦226064 ancestors to¦226065 enter¦226065 and¦226053 \add ≈take¦226066 ownership¦226066 of¦226066\add*.\x + \xo 9:23: a \xt Gen 15:5; 22:17; \xo b \xt Josh 3:14-17.\x*
\v 24 Their¦226082 children¦226069 went in and¦226070 \add ≈took¦226070 over\add* the¦226073 land¦226073 \add ≈after you¦226074 went ahead¦226075 of¦226070 them and¦226074\add* subdued¦226074 the¦226078 \add previous\add* inhabitants¦226078, the Canaanites¦226080. You¦226081 \add ≈allowed them to defeat\add* them and¦226083 their¦226085 kings¦226085, and¦226086 the¦226088 people¦226088 groups in the land—\add ≈letting them do whatever they¦226068 wanted\add* to do with¦226082 them¦226091.\x + \xo 9:24: \xt Josh 11:23.\x*
\v 25 They¦226094 captured¦226094 fortified¦226096 cities¦226095 and¦226097 \add ≈productive land¦226097\add*, and¦226099 they¦226099 \add ≈took¦226099 over\add* houses¦226100 full¦226101 of¦226103 all good¦226105 things¦226105, \add ≈stone\add* cisterns, vineyards¦226108 and¦226109 olive¦226109 orchards, and \add ≈lots of\add* fruit trees¦226109. They¦226113 ate¦226113 and¦226114 were¦226114 satisfied¦226114, and¦226115 grew¦226115 fat¦226115 and¦226116 \add ≈enjoyed themselves as a result of¦226117 your¦226117 amazing\add* goodness¦226117.\x + \xo 9:25: \xt Deu 6:10-11.\x*
\p
\v 26 “\add ≈But¦226120\add* they¦226120 disobeyed¦226120 and¦226121 rebelled¦226121 against you, and¦226123 they¦226123 \add ≈turned their¦226128 backs¦226128 on¦226136 your instructions¦226126\add*. They¦226132 killed¦226132 your prophets¦226131 who¦226133 testified¦226135 against them in¦226136 order¦226137 to bring¦226137 them¦226137 back¦226137 to¦226138 you¦226138 and¦226139 they¦226139 \add ≈badly insulted you\add*.\x + \xo 9:26-28: \xt Jdg 2:11-16.\x*
\v 27 \add ≈So¦226143\add* you¦226143 \add ≈allowed¦226145 their enemies to harass¦226145 and conquer¦226145\add* them. Then¦226143 in¦226144 the¦226148 time¦226148 of¦226148 their¦226149 distress¦226149, they¦226150 cried¦226150 out¦226150 to¦226151 you¦226151, and¦226152 you¦226154 yourself heard¦226154 from heaven¦226153. \add ≈Because you're so merciful\add*, you¦226157 \add ≈sent\add* saviours to¦226158 them¦226158 who rescued¦226160 them¦226160 from¦226161 their¦226162 enemies.
\v 28 After \add ≈they'd returned¦226166 to an era of peace\add*, they reverted to doing¦226167 evil¦226168 \add ≈again¦226175 in¦226171 front¦226169 of you\add* and¦226170 you¦226170 left¦226170 them¦226170 to \add ≈submit to\add* their¦226172 enemies¦226172 and \add ≈the¦226171 oppression that followed\add*. Then¦226164 they'd return¦226175 and¦226176 cry¦226176 out¦226176 to¦226176 you¦226176, and¦226177 you¦226179 heard¦226179 from¦226178 heaven¦226178 and¦226180 delivered them¦226180 many¦226182 times¦226183 \add ≈because you're merciful\add*.
\v 29 You¦226185 \add ≈showed them their errors so they'd return to following your¦226190 instructions¦226196, but¦226185 instead they ignored you¦226185\add* and didn't¦226193 \add ≈obey your commands¦226196\add*. \add ≈They¦226191 ignored your values which¦226201 would have helped them if they'd lived¦226205\add* by them¦226206 and¦226207 they¦226207 turned¦226207 a¦226208 stubborn¦226209 shoulder¦226208, stiffened¦226211 their necks¦226210, and¦226212 \add ≈refused to listen¦226213\add*.\x + \xo 9:29: \xt Lev 18:5.\x*
\v 30 \add ≈Yet\add* you¦226215 \add ≈put up\add* with them¦226216 for many¦226218 years¦226217, and¦226215 you¦226219 testified¦226219 against them¦226220 with your spirit¦226221 \add ≈through¦226221 the¦226222 messages\add* of¦226222 your prophets¦226224, but¦226215 they¦226226 \add still\add* didn't¦226225 \add ≈take any notice, so\add* you¦226227 \add ≈allowed the other people¦226229 groups to conquer\add* them.\x + \xo 9:30: \xt 2Ki 17:13-18; 2Ch 36:15-16.\x*
\v 31 \add ≈However, because¦226240 you're so merciful\add*, you didn't abandon¦226239 them and you didn't \add ≈wipe them out completely¦226237\add*. \add Yes,\add* you're a god¦226241 who's gracious¦226243 and¦226244 merciful.
\p
\v 32 “\add ≈So¦226247 now¦226247\add* God, our amazing, powerful¦226250, and¦226252 awesome¦226252 God who¦226253 keeps¦226253 \add ≈his agreements due to¦226259 his\add* loyal¦226255 commitment, don't¦226256 \add ≈just¦226280 ignore all our current hardships¦226263 affecting\add* us¦226266, our kings¦226267 and our¦226267 leaders¦226268, our¦226268 priests¦226269 and our prophets¦226270, and our ancestors¦226271 and¦226272 all¦226272 your¦226274 people¦226274, from the¦226275 \add ≈period\add* of¦226275 the¦226276 Assyrian kings¦226276 until¦226278 today.\x + \xo 9:32: \xt 2Ki 15:19-29; 17:3-6; Ezr 4:2,10.\x*
\v 33 You¦226292 are¦226283 \add ≈totally fair in allowing all¦226285 that¦226287 to happen to\add* us¦226288, because¦226289 you¦226292 have behaved faithfully¦226291, but¦226282 \add ≈in contrast\add*, we¦226293 have¦226294 behaved wickedly¦226294—
\v 34 and¦226296 our kings¦226298, our¦226298 leaders¦226299, our¦226299 priests¦226300, and our ancestors¦226301 haven't \add ≈obeyed your¦226304 instructions¦226309\add* and they¦226306 haven't \add ≈bothered with¦226313 following\add* your commands¦226309 or \add taking notice of\add* your \add ≈complaints that¦226311 you¦226312 made know to¦226307\add* them¦226313.
\v 35 \add ≈They¦226315 served¦226331 in¦226316 their¦226316 own¦226316 kingdom¦226316 and¦226317 enjoyed the¦226318 incredible¦226318 goodness¦226317 that you poured on¦226316\add* them¦226322 and¦226323 the wide¦226324 and prosperous land¦226323 that you gave¦226321 them, \add ≈but¦226315\add* they¦226331 didn't serve¦226331 you¦226331, and¦226332 they¦226334 didn't turn¦226334 away from¦226335 their¦226335 evil¦226336 actions¦226335.
\p
\v 36 “\add ≈Take¦226354 notice of¦226346\add* us today—we're servants, and the¦226342 land¦226342 that¦226343 you¦226345 gave¦226345 to¦226346 our¦226346 ancestors¦226346 \add ≈so we could\add* eat¦226347 its fruit¦226350 and its produce¦226350, \add ≈but¦226342 look at us now\add*—we're servants in \add @our¦226339 own¦226339 land¦226339\add*.
\v 37 \add ≈Now\add* its¦226359 plentiful produce¦226359 belongs to the kings¦226361 who¦226362 \add ≈you've¦226364 placed over¦226365 us¦226365 due to\add* our sins¦226366, and¦226367 who rule¦226369 over our bodies¦226368 and¦226370 over¦226370 our livestock¦226370 \add ≈just however they¦226369 want to¦226371, so\add* we're \add ≈terribly distressed¦226372\add*.
